# Paper <-> experiment contract for LGC-EGC (TMM / PR). BINDING, versioned.
# One source of truth: every number, table and figure of the paper must be listed in paper_elements, and every
# input it needs must be listed in artefacts. The checker (tools/eval/check_contract.py) enforces both.
# Change rule:
#   - Only the user changes this file.
#   - Every change gets a new `version`, a line in `changelog`, and a commit.
#   - After tag build38-amend2, a change is also a reported deviation.
#   - Coding agents never edit it.
version: "1.6"
date: "2026-10-12"
status: "FROZEN (2026-10-12, v1.6). Decisions D1-D10 confirmed by the user; the v1.6 sha256 is recorded in amendment 2 deviation D10."
changelog:
  - "1.0 2026-10-10 first version; reconciles experiment_framework, final/low-cost plans, reviewer-eval s6-7, manuscript s7"
  - "1.1 2026-10-10 user: checkpoints 100 200 500 1k 2k 2.5k 5k 10k (8); E4/E5/E8, I01, I09, disk updated; AUC unchanged"
  - "1.2 2026-10-11 user: Sign_OPT has no targeted mode (attack/Sign_OPT.py:370); methods.Sign_OPT.modes -> [non_targeted]"
  - "1.3 2026-10-11 user: HSJA and Sign_OPT removed from the run roster (D7: scope + compute, decided before any n = 200 result); cited only; E5, E16 and disk estimate updated"
  - "1.4 2026-10-11 user: D8 CGBA accounting fix (faithful model + boundary-walk query-count fix, B3b T2/T3; trajectory bit-identical; disclosed)"
  - "1.5 2026-10-12 user: E10 (Places365) and E11 (RobustBench R50) promoted to REQUIRED, both modes, n = 200 (D9); reduced roster for E10/E11; D5, disk and cost updated"
  - "1.6 2026-10-12 user: E10/E11 split sha256 and victim files registered (D10); EGC out_dir per (victim, mode)"

decisions:   # D-items resolved here; the user confirms or edits before FROZEN
  D1_budgets: >-
    (v1.1, user 2026-10-10)
    Every run records and stores ALL eight checkpoints: 100 200 500 1000 2000 2500 5000 10000.
    Roles:
      - 100 / 200 / 500 / 1000: low-query regime (E8; OPOQA-style table);
      - 2000 / 5000 / 10000: TtBA Table 1 format (E2);
      - 2500: CGBA alignment;
      - every checkpoint: curves (E4, E5).
    AUC stays the registered one, over 500 1000 2500 5000 10000; 100, 200 and 2000 are descriptive only.
    Checkpoints are observation-only in the engine (_fill_crossed / carry-forward). B0 proves this on the frozen tag:
    the 6 registered budgets must be bit-identical with and without the extra 100 / 200.
    If an attack's initialisation is not finished at 100 or 200, that row has found = 0 (no back-fill).
  D2_checkpoint_convention: >-
    Baselines (incl. TtBA via adapters/run_ttba_v2.py): best adversarial (min pixel L2) among all queries with index
    <= B, from the decision-only HardLabelTracker.
    LGC-EGC: the engine state at B (last completed iteration with q <= B).
    The baseline convention is never less favourable to the baseline than its own iterate, so the asymmetry can only
    favour the baselines. It is disclosed.
    The TtBA adapter also records the official iterate (pix_l2_iter) for the G3/G5 comparison with TtBA Table 1.
  D3_perceptual_asr: "ASR_perc uses LPIPS-vgg; NT (tau_L, tau_S) = (0.05, 0.99), T (0.3, 0.75); adversarial = adv_float"
  D4_ablations: >-
    Main-protocol ablations are NOT run. The ablation table uses existing confirm_37 data only (ResNet-50 V1, seed
    2718, n = 100, metrics pix_l2 / ssim / lpips-vgg; no stored images, so no DISTS / LPIPS-alex). It is labelled with
    that protocol.
    Rows: EGC, LGC_RC (no ambient block), EGCI (circle metric), HT1000 (naive switch).
    The operator-substitution row (PVR-E step in the A-block) is included only if its source CSV is found and
    hashed (E9b).
  D5_conditional_sections: >-
    E12 (low-query breadth table) remains CONDITIONAL: it is written only if its runs are approved
    after the B4/B4b cost table and pass the same artefact checks; otherwise the section is cut
    (no legacy numbers). E10 (Places365) and E11 (AT robust) were promoted to REQUIRED by D9 (v1.5).
  D6_failures: >-
    An image with status error, or not adversarial at B, counts as a failure for ASR (L2 = inf).
    Paired statistics use images where both methods are adversarial at B, and print the count excluded.
    Failures are never re-run selectively; an interrupted run is resumed only for images without a completed row.

  D7_baseline_scope: >-
    (v1.3, user 2026-10-11) HSJA and Sign_OPT are not run. Reason: scope (the comparison is
    restricted to recent prior-free decision-based attacks with official code: TtBA, ARS-OPT,
    CGBA / CGBA-H) and compute; Sign_OPT is also untargeted-only (attack/Sign_OPT.py:370).
    Decided before any n = 200 result was opened, not on B3 numbers (B3 HSJA / Sign-OPT numbers
    are unvalidated and never reported). Their published numbers may appear only in the E2
    dagger block (if ttba_table1.json contains them), never in E1, E3-E8, a statistic or a
    ratio with our results. adapters/run_hsja.py and run_signopt.py are kept for a possible
    descriptive appendix run during revision.

  D8_cgba_accounting_fix: >-
    (v1.4, user 2026-10-11) run_cgba.py uses (a) _faithful_model -- the normalised tensor goes straight
    into the raw un-normalised ResNet-50 exactly as the official drivers, removing the old
    UnnormalizeVictim float32 double-normalisation round-trip (B3b T2: a 2.384e-07 error flips a
    decision and diverges the trajectory; ratio reached 0.68/1.17); and (b) a PatchedProposedAttack
    subclass that corrects the official boundary-walk query count (proposed_attack.py:145/:165
    off-by-one at the 40-iteration cap: num_calls==40 after only 39 is_adversarial calls), which
    otherwise trips assert self.all_queries == q_num (proposed_attack.py:252) on non_targeted images.
    The returned boundary point is unchanged; B3b T3 proves the trajectory is bit-identical up to and
    past the crash point. Disclosed in the paper as "accounting fix, trajectory unchanged".

  D9_extra_datasets: >-
    (v1.5, user 2026-10-12) E10 (Places365) and E11 (AT robust) are REQUIRED, both modes, n = 200.
    E10 victims: resnet50_places365, densenet161_places365 (official MIT Places365, ImageNet
    normalisation). E11 victim: Salman2020Do_R50 (RobustBench, Linf, 64.02% clean / 34.96% robust,
    loaded via robustbench.utils.load_model). E10/E11 use the reduced roster
    {LGC_RC_EGC, TtBA, CGBA(NT)/CGBA_H(T)} to control cost (ARS_OPT is already shown on the main
    ImageNet study). Decided before any n = 200 result was opened on these datasets.

  D10_e10e11_registration: >-
    (v1.6, user 2026-10-12) Register the E10/E11 split sha256 and victim weight files in constants;
    ours uses one out_dir per (victim, mode) so NT and T never share env_frame.txt. Reported deviation
    before any E10/E11 n = 200 result is opened.

constants:
  budget: 10000
  checkpoints: [100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, 2500, 5000, 10000]
  registered_checkpoints: [500, 1000, 2000, 2500, 5000, 10000]   # prereg / build 38 command; used by the B0 bit-identity test
  auc_budgets: [500, 1000, 2500, 5000, 10000]
  auc_definition: "per-image mean of log(pix_l2) over auc_budgets (L2); mean of the metric over auc_budgets (LPIPS, DISTS, SSIM)"
  n_main: 200
  rows: "1-200 of splits/{imagenet/ttba_github,places365,robust}/{arch}_{mode}.csv (targeted: the first 200 pairs)"
  victims: {vgg19: vgg19-dcbb9e9d.pth, resnet50: resnet50-11ad3fa6.pth, vit_b_32: vit_b_32-d86f8d99.pth,
            resnet50_places365: resnet50_places365.pth.tar,
            densenet161_places365: densenet161_places365.pth.tar,
            Salman2020Do_R50: Salman2020Do_R50.pt}
  modes: [non_targeted, targeted]
  split_sha256:   # ImageNet: prereg_build38.txt lines 56-61; E10/E11: C2b report section 2 (D10)
    resnet50_non_targeted: e08a069e932e5162963794c5d1469a7554efb0641470f443d8337be9f12a6142
    resnet50_targeted: 550ec796e485b601aadbd8953a085a9466273bc8778311b5840a6e76e69caa34
    vgg19_non_targeted: 1e811637c264029425121870a88781a57ee67f2745fea16649e1ea03306671d9
    vgg19_targeted: cf0a8efb783de12f8f4f130137ca4b756c1fe048bb23fae5b366b0f1d49a3360
    vit_b_32_non_targeted: a5f152ec215aaac4efc266b863dad3841c7c6f5ff6aed651d973a213095959db
    vit_b_32_targeted: c5eee382244c0beddb10bdec40a19e9d2bd57ee47a54cd61ab10b11937337a7b
    resnet50_places365_non_targeted: 351bc50f594f7ddcf7746cf7769ffc3ea5329271b150d762099feed4bf60012f
    resnet50_places365_targeted: 70bd3d5c5989df6829b39a310a59203d6a5ee760f7481a5b213a2df49107eaaa
    densenet161_places365_non_targeted: 89252849771532358f422f0046f47b91c391429c77731993881946780166a547
    densenet161_places365_targeted: 51935b7522274cebd361b5b91e4649d18bb8da5af739010670e733b2efc4b790
    Salman2020Do_R50_non_targeted: 1b847d4c3acc858a992a202bbdc6120f525922a1a8a42a0be2c6575a480778a7
    Salman2020Do_R50_targeted: 2985ebc400ea2f292077f6c84dc809ef6591629bbd81e606b0c429a8c062d00a
  engine_sha256_prefix: 835f1933d9e5
  dev_overlap_rows_1_200: {vgg19: {non_targeted: 6, targeted: 7}, resnet50: {non_targeted: 4, targeted: 6}, vit_b_32: {non_targeted: 2, targeted: 4}}
  asr_l2: {non_targeted: 2.5, targeted: 12.0}
  asr_rmse: [0.1, 0.05, 0.01]          # RMSE = pix_l2 / sqrt(3*224*224); low-query table at 500 and 1000
  asr_perc: {lpips_net: vgg, non_targeted: {tau_L: 0.05, tau_S: 0.99}, targeted: {tau_L: 0.3, tau_S: 0.75}}
  stats: {bootstrap_B: 10000, ci: 0.95, test: wilcoxon_signed_rank, claims_sided: one, descriptive_sided: two, multiplicity: holm}
  adv_store: {dtype: float16, ADV_STORE_BUDGETS: "must be UNSET (store every checkpoint)"}
  metrics_offline: [l2, linf, psnr, ssim, ms_ssim, lpips_alex, lpips_vgg, dists, fsim]
  metric_roles: {primary: [lpips_vgg, lpips_alex, dists], secondary: [ssim], descriptive: [l2, ms_ssim, psnr, linf, fsim]}

methods:   # id = the `method` value written in every output file
  LGC_RC_EGC: {role: ours, modes: [non_targeted, targeted], producer: "ttba_github/run_frame_b1.sh (--split_csv, --save_adv)", convention: engine_state}
  TtBA:       {role: main, modes: [non_targeted, targeted], producer: adapters/run_ttba_v2.py, convention: tracker_best, extra_columns: [pix_l2_iter]}
  CGBA:       {role: main, modes: [non_targeted], producer: adapters/run_cgba.py, convention: tracker_best}
  CGBA_H:     {role: main, modes: [targeted], producer: adapters/run_cgba.py, convention: tracker_best}
  ARS_OPT:    {role: main, modes: [non_targeted, targeted], producer: adapters/run_arsopt.py, convention: tracker_best, condition: "prior-free mode exists (B1); else status CUT and listed in the threat-model table"}

cited_methods:   # never run, no artefacts; E2 dagger block only (D7)
  HSJA: {source: ttba_github/ttba_table1.json, element: E2_l2_table_ttba_format,
         block: dagger, condition: "rows present for that victim/mode/budget; else related work only"}
  Sign_OPT: {source: ttba_github/ttba_table1.json, element: E2_l2_table_ttba_format,
             block: dagger, condition: "as HSJA"}

artefacts:   # required for EVERY (method, victim, mode) cell of the main study; {n} = n_main
  per_checkpoint:
    file_glob: "<out>/<mode>/per_checkpoint*.csv"
    required_columns: [arch, mode, image, method, budget, found, state_query, pix_l2]
    recommended_columns: [pix_linf, adv_float, adv_uint8, ssim, lpips, source_label, target_label]
    rows_per_cell: "{n} x 8 (one per image and checkpoint, found = 0 rows included), none duplicated"
  runs:
    file_glob: "<out>/<mode>/runs*.csv"
    required_columns: [image, method, status, wall_time_s]
    rows_per_cell: "{n}"
  adv_store:
    x0: "<out>/<mode>/adv_store/<arch>/<image>/x0.npy (float32, shape (3,224,224), values in [0,1])"
    npz: "<out>/<mode>/adv_store/<arch>/<image>/<method>_Q<budget>.npz for every checkpoint with found = 1"
    npz_keys: [delta, budget, state_query, adv_flag, l2, linf, method, image, arch, mode]
    forbidden: "<out>/<mode>/adv_store/x0_mismatch.csv"
  env:
    files: ["<out>/env_frame.txt (ours)", "<out>/<mode>/env_<method>.json (baselines)"]
    must_contain: [git_commit_or_repo_commit, engine_sha256 (ours), split_csv_sha256, victim_weight_file, torch, cuda, gpu_name, budget, checkpoints]
  run_manifest:
    file: "<out>/<mode>/run_manifest.json (baselines; lgc-baselines F1-F12)"
  disk_estimate: "~0.48 GB per (method, victim, mode); main 24 cells ~11.5 GB + E10 12 cells ~5.8 GB + E11 6 cells ~2.9 GB = ~20 GB plus x0.npy; B4b/B5 must show >= 25 GB free"

invariants:   # each is a check in check_contract.py; id -> severity
  I01_all_checkpoints: {severity: FAIL, rule: "every (image, method) has exactly the 8 budgets of constants.checkpoints (found = 0 rows count)"}
  I02_image_set: {severity: FAIL, rule: "the image set of every cell equals the sources of rows 1-200 of the split CSV, in any order; no extra image"}
  I03_target_pairs: {severity: FAIL, rule: "targeted: target_label (if present) equals the split CSV target_label of that source"}
  I04_query_budget: {severity: FAIL, rule: "state_query <= budget for every row; runs total queries <= 10000"}
  I05_npz_present: {severity: FAIL, rule: "an npz exists for every row with found = 1; its keys include npz_keys; budget and method match the file name"}
  I06_l2_consistency: {severity: FAIL, rule: "|npz l2 - pix_l2| / pix_l2 < 1e-3, and |npz l2 - ||delta||_2 recomputed| / l2 < 1e-3"}
  I07_x0_identity: {severity: FAIL, rule: "no x0_mismatch.csv; x0.npy shape (3,224,224), finite, in [0,1]"}
  I08_monotone: {severity: FAIL_for_tracker_best / WARN_for_engine_state, rule: "pix_l2 is non-increasing in budget for every (image, method) with found = 1"}
  I09_found_targeted: {severity: WARN, rule: "targeted rows have found = 1 from the first budget after the start is verified; report per method the share of found = 0 at 100 and 200 (both modes)"}
  I10_env_lock: {severity: FAIL, rule: "split sha256 = constants.split_sha256; engine sha prefix; one GPU name and torch version across all cells"}
  I11_adv_store_env: {severity: FAIL, rule: "ADV_STORE_BUDGETS unset and dtype float16 recorded in env"}
  I12_no_legacy: {severity: FAIL, rule: "no input path contains Images_without95%, Without95%, v2_submitted or legacy npz results"}
  I13_metrics_complete: {severity: FAIL, rule: "metrics CSV has one row per stored npz, every column of constants.metrics_offline finite, l2_relerr < 1e-3"}
  I14_elements_complete: {severity: FAIL, rule: "every REQUIRED paper element has all its inputs; every CONDITIONAL element is either complete or marked CUT"}
  I15_macros: {severity: FAIL, rule: "every \\Num macro used in paper/v3 is defined in generated/numbers.tex and traced in summary_*.json; no '??' left"}

paper_elements:   # E-id: what the paper shows -> exactly what data it needs
  E1_main_perceptual_table:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "per victim x mode: methods x {LPIPS-vgg, LPIPS-alex, DISTS, SSIM, L2} mean (median) at 10000"
    inputs: {source: metrics_csv, budgets: [10000], methods: main+ours, cells: all6}
  E2_l2_table_ttba_format:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "mean (median) pix_l2 at 2000 / 5000 / 10000 and ASR at L2 <= 2.5 (NT) / 12 (T), 10000; cited TtBA Table 1 rows in a separate dagger block"
    inputs: {source: per_checkpoint, budgets: [2000, 5000, 10000], methods: main+ours, cells: all6, external: ttba_github/ttba_table1.json}
  E3_paired_stats_table:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "ours vs each baseline: LPIPS-vgg AUC delta, DISTS AUC delta, L2 AUC ratio, L2@10k ratio [95% CI], Holm star, W/L; n printed"
    inputs: {source: [metrics_csv, per_checkpoint], budgets: "auc_budgets + [10000]", methods: main+ours, cells: all6}
  E4_asr_perc:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "table of ASR_perc at 1000 / 10000 + curve over all 8 checkpoints + ASR vs threshold sweep (LPIPS, SSIM) at 10000"
    inputs: {source: metrics_csv, budgets: checkpoints, methods: main+ours, cells: all6}
  E5_curves:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "median (IQR) pix_l2 and LPIPS-vgg vs queries at the 8 checkpoints (log-x 100..10000), same resolution for every method (traces not used)"
    inputs: {source: [per_checkpoint, metrics_csv], budgets: checkpoints, methods: main+ours, cells: all6}
  E6_pareto:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "per-image (L2, LPIPS-vgg) at 10000, ours vs each baseline, small multiples"
    inputs: {source: metrics_csv, budgets: [10000], methods: main+ours, cells: all6}
  E7_comparison_grid:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "clean | each method's adversarial | 0.5 + amp * delta with one amplification per row; metric values under each image; rule-based image choice saved in a caption file"
    inputs: {source: adv_store+metrics_csv, budgets: [1000, 10000], methods: main+ours, cells: "all6 (3 images each)"}
  E8_low_query_table:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "found rate, ASR at RMSE 0.1 / 0.05 / 0.01, median pix_l2 and median LPIPS-vgg at 100 / 200 / 500 / 1000"
    inputs: {source: [per_checkpoint, metrics_csv], budgets: [100, 200, 500, 1000], methods: main+ours, cells: all6}
  E9_ablation_table:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "confirm_37 rows (D4), labelled 'ResNet-50 V1, seed 2718, n = 100'; pix_l2 AUC and 10k ratio, SSIM, LPIPS-vgg"
    inputs: {source: "confirm_37 result CSVs (path + sha256 recorded in reports/E9_sources.md)", metrics: [pix_l2, ssim, lpips]}
  E9b_operator_substitution:
    status: CONDITIONAL
    content: "EGC with a PVR-E / TtBA step in the A-block vs EGC"
    inputs: {source: "the run that produced 1.001 NT / 1.003 T: locate CSV + sha256, else CUT"}
  E10_places365:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "cross-dataset generalization on Places365-Standard val_256 (365 classes); per-victim x per-mode
              tables (E1-E8 format) for resnet50_places365 and densenet161_places365"
    inputs:
      victims: [resnet50_places365, densenet161_places365]
      modes: [non_targeted, targeted]
      n: 200
      methods: [LGC_RC_EGC, TtBA, CGBA, CGBA_H]
      sources:
        resnet50_places365: "http://places2.csail.mit.edu/models_places365/resnet50_places365.pth.tar"
        densenet161_places365: "http://places2.csail.mit.edu/models_places365/densenet161_places365.pth.tar"
        data: "http://data.csail.mit.edu/places/places365/val_256.tar"
  E11_robust_model:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "robustness against an adversarially trained ResNet-50 (RobustBench); per-mode tables (E1-E8 format)"
    inputs:
      victims: [Salman2020Do_R50]
      modes: [non_targeted, targeted]
      n: 200
      methods: [LGC_RC_EGC, TtBA, CGBA, CGBA_H]
      sources:
        Salman2020Do_R50: "RobustBench Linf (NeurIPS 2020), 64.02% clean / 34.96% robust"
  E12_low_query_breadth:
    status: CONDITIONAL
    inputs: {mode: non_targeted, budget: 1000, extra_victims: "to be named", n: 200}
  E13_cost_table:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "seconds per image (sequential runs, same GPU), queries; decoder JVPs per image ONLY if the runner records them (else that column is omitted and the text does not claim it)"
    inputs: {source: runs, cells: all6}
  E14_selection_and_sensitivity:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "protocol facts from reports/P2_selection_audit.md; every E3 claim recomputed without dev-overlap rows; class-balanced variant (descriptive)"
    inputs: {source: [P2 report, metrics_csv, per_checkpoint, overlap_dev_seeds.json]}
  E15_fairness_provenance_table:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "generated/tables/fairness.tex from env/manifest files (lgc-baselines B7)"
    inputs: {source: [env, run_manifest]}
  E16_threat_model_table:
    status: REQUIRED
    content: "text-only table (no numbers from runs): (a) methods excluded by the threat model (surrogates / priors) and why; (b) methods excluded by scope (HSJA, Sign_OPT; cited only, D7)"
    inputs: {source: none}
